{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21eb7e39d99b57bc5aaa", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Rotational Motion - Test 6", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 40, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242f0c"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242f09", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e93", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9259"], "question": {"text": "Two discs of same mass and different radii are made of different materials such that their thicknesses are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> respectively. The densities of materials are in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. The moment of inertia of these discs respectively about their diameters will be in the ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "ec39ef", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e94"}, {"id": "029b4f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e95"}, {"id": "05baf0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e96"}, {"id": "eb58f8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e97"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e98", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0e3"], "question": {"text": "<p>A uniform disc with mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is mounted on a fixed horizontal axle as shown in figure. A block with mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> hangs from a massless cord that is wrapped around the rim of the disc. During the fall of the block, the cord does not slip and there is no friction at the axle. The tension in the cord is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.</p><p>(Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F8b286632-aa6f-4e93-9443-6cc00f86c4d2-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 166px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b0307d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e99"}, {"id": "6a405d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e9a"}, {"id": "80c8f8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e9b"}, {"id": "77236c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e9c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e9d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87cd"], "question": {"text": "A thin solid disk of 1 kg is rotating along its diameter axis at the speed of 1800 rpm. By applying an external torque of $25 \\pi \\mathrm{Nm}$ for 40 s, the speed increases to 2100 rpm. The diameter of the disk is ________ m."}, "options": [{"id": "aadcc6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e9e"}, {"id": "ebb43b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242e9f"}, {"id": "d91970", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ea0"}, {"id": "41d19a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ea1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ea2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0f"], "question": {"text": "<p>A ball of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> moving with a velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis, hits another ball of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> which is at rest. After the collision, the first ball comes to rest and the second one disintegrates into two equal pieces. One of the pieces starts moving along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>-axis at a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The second piece starts moving at a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> (degree) with respect to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis. The configuration of pieces after the collision is shown in the figure. The value of $\\theta$ to the nearest integer is _________.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F0a8aacf2-ca23-46e9-a541-464f20f935e1-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 248px; height: 228px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "df7050", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ea3"}, {"id": "fb357e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ea4"}, {"id": "ecec18", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ea5"}, {"id": "5f14b3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ea6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ea7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566f"], "concepts": ["617aa9c0ef3fe65ad8e81259"], "question": {"text": "Two discs of moment of inertia <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> about their central axes &amp; normal to their planes, rotating with angular speeds <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>rad</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo> </mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi>rad</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively are brought into contact face to face with their axe of rotation coincident. The loss in kinetic energy of the system in the process is _________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "e6fee4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ea8"}, {"id": "130c65", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ea9"}, {"id": "91aab4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eaa"}, {"id": "331309", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eab"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eac", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cae"], "question": {"text": "<p>A solid cylinder is released from rest from the top of an inclined plane of inclination <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. If the cylinder rolls without slipping, its speed upon reaching the bottom of the inclined plane is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff1512277-f579-41e7-9318-318cf103cbfb-9896745.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 295px; height: 200px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "afefd1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ead"}, {"id": "d666e5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eae"}, {"id": "98bf03", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eaf"}, {"id": "52bebb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eb0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eb1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["6162faec6ed13040ec84909e"], "concepts": ["617aa9c0ef3fe65ad8e81249"], "question": {"text": "A solid sphere of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is making pure rolling on a horizontal surface with kinetic energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2240</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. The velocity of centre of mass of the sphere will be ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "94690b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eb2"}, {"id": "05681e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eb3"}, {"id": "984577", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eb4"}, {"id": "a9f1cc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eb5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eb6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["6117b96d67dbe2603c3e9e09"], "question": {"text": "<p><math><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></math> is a plane lamina of the shape of an equilateral triangle. <math><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></math> are mid-points of <math><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></math> and <math><mi>G</mi></math> is the centroid of the lamina. Moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis passing through <math><mi>G</mi></math> and perpendicular to the plane <math><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></math> is <math><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></math>. If part <math><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow></math> is removed, the moment of inertia of the remaining part about the same axis is <math><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> where <math><mi>N</mi></math> is an integer. Value of <math><mi>N</mi></math> is:</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fbf713175-08d5-4dc1-8547-7dd0460fb38d-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 109px; height: 110px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "6e8462", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eb7"}, {"id": "551fa9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eb8"}, {"id": "b000a8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eb9"}, {"id": "bcdf75", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eba"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ebb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d48"], "question": {"text": "A cube having a side of 10 cm with unknown mass and 200 gm mass were hung at two ends of an uniform rigid rod of 27 cm long. The rod along with masses was placed on a wedge keeping the distance between wedge point and 200 gm weight as 25 cm. Initially the masses were not at balance. A beaker is placed beneath the unknown mass and water is added slowly to it. At given point the masses were in balance and half volume of the unknown mass was inside the water.<br/>(Take the density of unknown mass is more than that of the water, the mass did not absorb water and water density is $1 \\mathrm{gm} / \\mathrm{cm}^3$.) The unknown mass is ________ kg."}, "options": [{"id": "0d745f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ebc"}, {"id": "ff8b70", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ebd"}, {"id": "2603d5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ebe"}, {"id": "a567cc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ebf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ec0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b55"], "question": {"text": "<p>A solid cylinder length is suspended symmetrically through two massless strings, as shown in the figure. The distance from the initial rest position, the cylinder should be&nbsp;unbinding the strings to achieve a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, is _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p><p>(take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F0961315a-4ab4-40dc-995a-2ccf7ba1626f-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 128px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e69389", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ec1"}, {"id": "e14472", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ec2"}, {"id": "b99c57", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ec3"}, {"id": "12ae25", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ec4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ec5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["6176f3fb6581241c7072b5e7"], "question": {"text": "<p>A solid sphere is rolling on a horizontal plane without slipping. If the ratio of angular momentum about axis of rotation of the sphere to the total energy of moving sphere is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>22</mn></math> then, the value of its angular speed will be<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_________rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9fad3a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ec6"}, {"id": "882357", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ec7"}, {"id": "1a9da7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ec8"}, {"id": "6922ad", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ec9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eca", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b473f"], "question": {"text": "<p>A uniform disc of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> is projected with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> on a rough horizontal surface. It starts off with a purely sliding motion at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. After <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> it acquires a purely rolling motion (see figure). The total kinetic energy of the disc after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> will be ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>.</p><p>(given, coefficient of friction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>).</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb9e9713e-0ecf-4807-aa51-c40dbdf08273-9895955.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 168px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "56deba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ecb"}, {"id": "a1ec46", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ecc"}, {"id": "31bfb2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ecd"}, {"id": "d1e3f2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ece"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ecf", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e80a0"], "question": {"text": "A uniform thin bar of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math> meter is bent to make an equilateral hexagon. The moment of inertia about an axis passing through the centre of mass and perpendicular to the plane of hexagon is ___________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "f1d5ac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ed0"}, {"id": "34157a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ed1"}, {"id": "f3b67c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ed2"}, {"id": "59063b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ed3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ed4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e42"], "question": {"text": "A circular disc reaches from top to bottom of an inclined plane of length $l$. When it slips down the plane, if takes $t \\mathrm{~s}$. When it rolls down the plane then it takes $\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)^{1 / 2} t \\mathrm{~s}$, where $\\alpha$ is _________"}, "options": [{"id": "6886d0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ed5"}, {"id": "97745d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ed6"}, {"id": "be99ed", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ed7"}, {"id": "977979", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ed8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ed9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d48"], "question": {"text": "A force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">k</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> acts at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">i</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">j</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. Then the magnitude of torque about the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">j</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">k</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is.........."}, "options": [{"id": "a0fd20", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eda"}, {"id": "15cdd0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242edb"}, {"id": "9d9ce4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242edc"}, {"id": "37fd3e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242edd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ede", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0f"], "question": {"text": "A solid sphere with uniform density and radius R is rotating initially with constant angular velocity $\\left(\\omega_1\\right)$ about its diameter. After some time during the rotation its starts loosing mass at a uniform rate, with no change in its shape. The angular velocity of the sphere when its radius become $R / 2$ is $x \\omega_1$. The value of $x$ is ________"}, "options": [{"id": "f7e646", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242edf"}, {"id": "30b7c3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ee0"}, {"id": "671bb3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ee1"}, {"id": "44d83a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ee2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ee3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cae"], "question": {"text": "<p>A solid disc of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;rolls down without slipping on an inclined plane making an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> with the horizontal. The acceleration of the disc will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>g</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> is _______.&nbsp; (Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p><p>(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo></math> acceleration due to gravity)</p><p>(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo></math> angle as shown in figure)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F19b63ced-6c0c-4120-97dc-0d7e6d90a868-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 192px; height: 170px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "5a2c53", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ee4"}, {"id": "1868fb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ee5"}, {"id": "c518c3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ee6"}, {"id": "a7b236", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ee7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ee8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["6117b94a67dbe2603c3e992e"], "question": {"text": "The radius of gyration of a cylindrical rod about an axis of rotation perpendicular to its length and passing through the center will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Given, the length of the rod is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "3d8a73", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ee9"}, {"id": "dc2739", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eea"}, {"id": "5e6c0e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eeb"}, {"id": "4f8103", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eec"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eed", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e49"], "question": {"text": "<p>Consider a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> uniform circular disk of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. It is pin supported at its center and is at rest initially. The disk is acted upon by a constant force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> through a massless string wrapped around its periphery as shown in the figure.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F1ca5eaeb-c65e-4805-bdb7-65d34dd67ebd-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 178px; height: 218px;\" /></p><p>Suppose the disk makes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> number of revolutions to attain an angular speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>, to the nearest integer, is _______ .</p><p>[Given : In one complete revolution, the disk rotates by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7176f6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eee"}, {"id": "54bd42", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242eef"}, {"id": "6a9359", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ef0"}, {"id": "c76938", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ef1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ef2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0e3"], "question": {"text": "<p>A force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> is applied on an intersection point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;plane and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis. The magnitude of torque of this force about a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is ________.</p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "f063cf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ef3"}, {"id": "dcc3d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ef4"}, {"id": "44148d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ef5"}, {"id": "138250", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242ef6"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:53.109Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:53.109Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9242f0b"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures":